From 5ecebfc1372e7d9098d3d1a622e01e70d5167267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:06:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/70] ppc32: MinF64/MaxF64 load the zero they compare against

The pre-POWER7 fallbacks of MinF64/MaxF64 (the ppc32 branch restored
by the macro-assembler commit; ppc64 uses xsmindp/xsmaxdp) test the
"both operands compare equal" case for zero with

    fcmpu(lhs, kDoubleRegZero);

relying on d14 holding 0.0.  JSEntry loads it ("Set up the reserved
register for 0.0") and TurboFan never allocates d14, so the invariant
holds as long as only TurboFan, CSA builtins and the interpreter run.
Maglev breaks it: Assembler::DefaultFPTmpList() is {d13, d14}, and
MaglevAssembler::TemporaryRegisterScope hands d14 out as the second
scratch double (any node that acquires two FP temporaries, or one
inside a scope that already holds d13).  After the first such Maglev
code ran, every MinF64/MaxF64 on the thread - Maglev's Float64Min/Max
nodes, TurboFan's kPPC_MinDouble/kPPC_MaxDouble, the CSA Math.min/max
builtins, Turboshaft's DoubleArrayMinMax - compares against garbage
until the next JSEntry: max(-0, +0) can return -0, and max(x, x)
returns 2x whenever the garbage equals x.

Load 0.0 into the helper's `scratch` double register instead.  Every
caller passes kScratchDoubleReg (d13) for it - TurboFan explicitly,
Maglev through the default argument - which is never an allocatable
register, so it cannot alias lhs (DCHECKed); the later uses of
`scratch` in MinF64 overwrite it anyway.  The literal load costs a
few instructions on the equal-operands path only.  The other
kDoubleRegZero readers (CanonicalizeNaN, the Maglev
CompareDoubleAndJumpIfZeroOrNaN pair) already load it first.

Prerequisite of the ppc32 Maglev layer; no behavior change while
Maglev is off.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
index e8b23bf..4dbdf89 100644
--- a/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
+++ b/v8/src/codegen/ppc/macro-assembler-ppc.cc
@@ -2032,7 +2032,9 @@ void MacroAssembler::MinF64(DoubleRegister dst, DoubleRegister lhs,
   b(&return_right);
 
   bind(&check_zero);
-  fcmpu(lhs, kDoubleRegZero);
+  DCHECK(!AreAliased(scratch, lhs));
+  LoadDoubleLiteral(scratch, base::Double(0.0), r0);
+  fcmpu(lhs, scratch);
   /* left == right != 0. */
   bne(&return_left);
   /* At this point, both left and right are either 0 or -0. */
@@ -2089,7 +2091,9 @@ void MacroAssembler::MaxF64(DoubleRegister dst, DoubleRegister lhs,
   b(&return_right);
 
   bind(&check_zero);
-  fcmpu(lhs, kDoubleRegZero);
+  DCHECK(!AreAliased(scratch, lhs));
+  LoadDoubleLiteral(scratch, base::Double(0.0), r0);
+  fcmpu(lhs, scratch);
   /* left == right != 0. */
   bne(&return_left);
   /* At this point, both left and right are either 0 or -0. */
